"""Module 2: model chooses work; program does not auto-advance before choice."""
from exchange_core import packed
PROMPT='''Choose exactly ONE next work using CURRENT_EFFECTIVE_SPECIFICATION, current constraints and feedback. initial_request_history_only is NOT the current request after superseding permission. Original purchased SKU is the object returned, never confuse it with replacement SKU. Return JSON {"work_type":"query|analyze|clarify|prepare|confirm|submit|stop","object":"exact product ID for query; original_item_id for analyze/clarify; order_id for prepare/confirm/submit/stop","parameters":{},"evidence_refs":[integer actual history refs],"expected":"specific completion condition","reason":"brief grounded reason"}. Only clarify needs parameters={"variant_id":"observed feasible offer"}. For other works parameters={} (program uses current state; contradicting SKU parameters are rejected).
prepare only stores a FEASIBLE CURRENT plan; it does not resolve conflict, produce a diagnostic draft or seek relaxed conditions. If current request conflicts, use analyze (empty exact-match is a valid result), clarify a negotiable option, acquire genuinely missing evidence, or explain a justified stop if no continuation is possible. Optional analysis need not precede a grounded feasible clarification. Once current plan is stored and authorization missing, CONFIRM asks the actual user; re-prepare unchanged plan is redundant. Specification permission is not full approval. Only current complete-plan approval permits submit. Read execution rejection before retrying; do not repeat a known-rejected job. Never silently switch back to historical request. Multiple reasonable works may be acceptable.'''
def choose(w,t,group='direct'):
 return t.json([{'role':'system','content':PROMPT+'\n'+w.policy},{'role':'user','content':packed(w.model_state(group=='candidate'))}],'cognitive','next_work_choice')
